tively means you are "playing the board" with a 9 kicker. The opponent has checked on the pre-flop, flop, and turn, indicating weakness or a trap, but most likely they do not have a strong hand like an Ace or a 6. However, your hand has very little showdown value and virtually no potential to improve significantly on the river. Betting here turns your hand into a bluff, but since the pot is small and your hand has zero equity if called, risking chips is unnecessary.\n\nReason: Checking is the safest play. It allows you to see the River card for free without risking additional chips with a very weak hand. Since the opponent checked, there is no pressure to fold, and checking keeps the pot small, preserving your stack for better opportunities in the remaining hands of the match.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
