10). Your opponent has played passively, checking the Flop and calling the Turn, suggesting a marginal hand or a draw. Betting now yields thin value; worse hands may fold, while better hands (Flush, Straight, Full House) will call or raise. Checking is the prudent play to realize your showdown value without exposing yourself to a raise on a scary board.\n\nReason: The river card completes potential flush and straight draws. While trips are strong, your hand effectively plays the board for kickers. Checking minimizes loss against superior hands while still winning against the opponent's likely range of weaker pairs or missed draws.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
