n re-evaluate if called.\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: I hold Top Pair (Aces) with a 9 kicker on a board of 2h, 4d, As, Ks. The turn King brings a flush draw (spades) and connects with some second-best hands (Kx). The opponent has played passively (limp pre-flop, check-call flop, check turn), which usually indicates a marginal made hand (weak Ace, pocket pair, or now a King) or a draw. Checking back gives a free card to flush and straight draws. Betting extracts value from worse Aces and Kings that might call, and protects my hand equity. A bet of 200 (half pot) is a standard size to get value from worse hands while denying correct odds to draws.\n\nReason: My hand is strong relative to the opponent's passive line. Betting builds the pot when I am likely ahead and charges the opponent to see the river, preventing them from realizing their equity for free with draws.\n\nAnswer: 200"}
